      "round_summary": "Repair round 1/1 — handled failing property `passTokenMutex` (error_type: dut_bug). Root cause: all three Controller modules initalized passTokenReg to true.B, causing all three passToken outputs to be high at reset and violating mutual exclusion. Fix: added a `hasInitialToken: Boolean = false` parameter to the Controller class, changed `RegInit(true.B)` to `RegInit(if (hasInitialToken) true.B else false.B)`, and in Main instantiated controllerA with `hasInitialToken = true`, controllerB/controllerC with `hasInitialToken = false`. This ensures exactly one controller holds the token at reset, preserving the passTokenMutex invariant. The failing assertion label `passTokenMutex` is preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions exist because this is a DUT bug, not an assertion error — the `ackImpliesReq` assertion (also failing) is structurally independent and will be addressed in a subsequent round if needed.",
